L204: **DEFINITION OF VARIABLES**
L205: MEF40 is a term used by S&S. In the current terminology it corresponds to FEF60
L206: MEF40(P) is named below as FEF60(P) [which means MEF40 measured from on partial flow volume curve]
L207: **Variables published by S&S:**
L208: NO   = Participant number in the S&S report
L209: PlCh  = Placebo day:  Change in FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) **5 min** after exercise (from S&S Table III)
L210: VcCh  = Vitamin C day: Change in FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) **5 min** after exercise (from S&S Table III)
L211: PlBase = Placebo day:  baseline (pre-exercise) FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) level (from S&S Table V)
L212: VcBase = Vitamin C day: baseline (pre-exercise) FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) level (from S&S Table V)
L213: **The following are calculated from the above data:**
L214: P_D    = change on the placebo day:  PlCh/PlBase - 1 (in % units)
L215: VC_D    = change on the vitamin C day: VcCh/VcBase - 1 (in % units)
L216: Eff_VitC_x = Effect of vitamin C in percentage points: P_D - VC_D
L217: (x indicates FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P))
L218: Base_D   = Difference in baseline levels between placebo and vitamin C days: PlBase - VcBase
L219: PlEnd   = Placebo day:  Postexercise level of FEF60/FEF60(P): PlBase - PlCh
L220: VcEnd   = Vitamin C day: Postexercise level of FEF60/FEF60(P): VcBase - VcCh
L221: End_Ratio = Effect of vitamin C on postexercise FEF60/FEF60(P) level:
L222: (VcEnd/PlEnd) - 1 (in % units)
L223: _ed    = Small changes are made in the data points to avoid overlapping in Figs
L224: (but the statistical models are based on the actual data and not on the edited data)
L225: **************************************************************************************
L226: The statistical models on the following pages were constructed by using the R-package:
L227: [http://www.r-project.org/](http://www.r-project.org/)
L228: Likelihood ratio (LR) test was used to compare two statistical models to find out
L229: whether the addition of a new variable improves the model significantly.
L230: For a short description of the LR test:
L231: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Likelihood-ratio_test](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Likelihood-ratio_test)
L232: In the comparison of two statistical models, a large χ [2] value (a small P-value) means that
L233: the added variable significantly improves the regression model.
