L559: 7
L560: **Figs. 2E-F. Effect of vitamin C on the 5-min postexercise FEF60(P)**
L561: In Figs. 2E and 2F the dash lines indicate equality between vitamin C and placebo.
L562: If vitamin C has no effect, the observations would be located randomly and symmetrically
L563: on both sides of the dash lines. The continuous lines indicate the regression lines.
L564: The numbers identify the participants with the same numbers as used by S&S.
L565: **2E: Vitamin C effect on postexercise FEF60(P) change.**
L566: This figure shows the effect of vitamin C in percentage points (pp).
L567: For example, on the placebo-day, participant #11 had a FEF60(P) change of -93.33%,
L568: and on the vitamin C day a FEF60(P) change of -66.67%,
L569: which gives the 27 pp improvement shown in Fig. 2E.
L570: Slope of the linear regression model indicates that postexercise FEF60(P) change was decreased
L571: by 63% (95% CI: 29% to 97%) on the vitamin C day compared with the change on the placebo day.
L572: Addition of the placebo-day postexercise FEF60(P) change to the model containing the intercept
L573: improved the model fit by χ [2] (1 df) = 12.0 (P = 0.0005).
L574: **2F: Vitamin C effect on postexercise FEF60(P) level.**
L575: This figure shows the effect of vitamin C in percentages.
L576: For example, on the placebo-day, participant #11 had a postexercise FEF60(P) level of 0.2 L/s,
L577: and on the vitamin C day a postexercise FEF60(P) level of 0.6 L/s,
L578: which gives the 200% increase in the postexercise FEF60(P) level shown in Fig. 2F.
L579: Addition of the placebo-day postexercise FEF60(P) level to the model containing the intercept
L580: improved the model fit by χ [2] (1 df) = 9.7 (P = 0.002). Addition of the spline knot at 1.1 L/s
L581: further improved the fit by χ [2] (1 df) = 15.9 (P = 0.0001). Simultaneous addition of the two spline
L582: segments with the knot at 1.1 L/s to the model containing only the intercept improved
L583: the model fit by χ [2] (2 df) = 25.6 (P = 0.000003).
