L755: 1
L756: **DEFINITION OF VARIABLES**
L757: MEF40 is a term used by S&S. In the current terminology it corresponds to FEF60
L758: MEF40(P) is named below as FEF60(P), which means MEF40 based on a partial flow volume curve
L759: **Variables published by S&S:**
L760: NO   = Participant number in the S&S report
L761: PlCh  = Placebo day:  Change in FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) **0 min** after exercise (from S&S Table II)
L762: VcCh  = Vitamin C day: Change in FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) **0 min** after exercise (from S&S Table II)
L763: PlBase = Placebo day:  baseline (pre-exercise) FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) level (from S&S Table V)
L764: VcBase = Vitamin C day: baseline (pre-exercise) FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P) level (from S&S Table V)
L765: **The following are calculated from the above data:**
L766: P_D    = change on the placebo day:  PlCh/PlBase - 1 (in % units)
L767: VC_D    = change on the vitamin C day: VcCh/VcBase - 1 (in % units)
L768: Eff_VitC_x = Effect of vitamin C in percentage points: P_D - VC_D
L769: (x indicates FEV1/PEF/FEF60/FEF60(P))
L770: Base_D   = Difference in baseline levels between placebo and vitamin C days: PlBase - VcBase
L771: PlEnd   = Placebo day:  Postexercise level of FEF60/FEF60(P): PlBase - PlCh
L772: VcEnd   = Vitamin C day: Postexercise level of FEF60/FEF60(P): VcBase - VcCh
L773: End_Ratio = Effect of vitamin C on postexercise FEF60/FEF60(P) level:
L774: (VcEnd/PlEnd) - 1 (in % units)
L775: _ed    = Small changes are made in the data points to avoid overlapping in Figs
L776: (but the statistical models are based on the actual data and not on the edited data)
L777: **************************************************************************************
L778: The statistical models on the following pages were constructed by using the R-package:
L779: [http://www.r-project.org/](http://www.r-project.org/)
L780: Likelihood ratio (LR) test was used to compare two statistical models to find out
L781: whether the addition of a new variable improves the model significantly.
L782: For a short description of the LR test:
L783: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Likelihood-ratio_test](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Likelihood-ratio_test)
L784: In the comparison of two statistical models, a large χ [2] value (a small P-value) means that
L785: the added variable significantly improves the regression model.
L786: 2
